我永远不会忘记。

282
00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:58.400
It was so bizarre.
那真是太离奇了。

283
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:05.500
So, you know, normally the Emmys, it's like in a traditional type theater where you sit in theater style seating, right?
你知道，通常艾美奖是在那种传统的剧院里，座位是剧院式的，对吧？

284
00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.240
One row in front of the other.
一排排坐在前面。

285
00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:12.140
Well, this year, it's like the Television Academy decided to mix it up.
但那一年，电视学院决定搞点新花样。

286
00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:15.020
And they put the seats in a circle.
他们把座位排成了一个圆圈。

287
00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:17.480
And the stage in the middle, a big circle.
舞台在中间，一个大圆圈。

288
00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.220
So, it was like theater in the round.
所以，就像是环形剧场。

289
00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:22.320
And, Jenna, I remember where we were seated.
而且，珍娜，我记得我们坐在哪儿。

290
00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:25.840
Oh, I knew the minute we took our seats, I wasn't going to win.
噢，我们一坐下我就知道，我肯定没戏了。

291
00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.000
Oh, honey.
噢，亲爱的。

292
00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.980
We were in the back of the circle.
我们坐在圆圈的后方。

293
00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:34.680
So, we faced everyone's butt all night.
所以，我们整晚都对着所有人的屁股。

294
00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:38.120
All night, we just saw real fancy people's asses.
整整一晚上，我们看到的都是大人物们的屁股。

295
00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.180
That's what we saw.
我们看到的就只有这些。

296
00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:45.600
And we kept thinking, at some point, are they going to turn around and face our section?
我们一直在想，他们什么时候会转过身来面对我们这一区呢？

297
00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:46.420
No.
没有。

298
00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:47.640
Never once.
一次都没有。

299
00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:53.060
The entire thing was performed as if there were not people sitting behind the speaker.
整场活动表演得好像坐在演讲者身后的人根本不存在一样。

300
00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.560
It was so bizarre.
那真是太离奇了。

301
00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:59.440
And, you know, sometimes someone who would win would, like, sort of glance over their shoulder, like,
