而我给自己的解释是，很明显，我在找更多那种奇怪的蓝色螺旋

755
00:36:10.640 --> 00:36:13.260
thingies that I'm going to hang in the conference room later.
小玩意儿，我待会儿要挂在会议室里。

756
00:36:14.440 --> 00:36:19.420
She had a vision of blue spiral thingies and she needed more of them.
她脑子里想的是蓝色螺旋小玩意儿，她需要更多这种东西。

757
00:36:19.580 --> 00:36:21.180
And so she's digging and digging.
所以她一直在翻找。

758
00:36:21.460 --> 00:36:24.460
But who uses this as a pickup line?
但谁会把这个当成搭讪的话术啊？

759
00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:28.600
Who thinks that a woman is going to like stop everything she's doing in your and just
谁会觉得一个女人会停下手里所有的事，然后

760
00:36:28.600 --> 00:36:29.420
be like, you're right.
说，你说得对。

761
00:36:29.600 --> 00:36:32.240
There's not dinner and a movie in this box.
这个盒子里可没有晚餐和电影。

762
00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:38.060
Oh, well, lady, we also have a fan catch here from Abby Tilford.
哦，好吧，女士，我们这里还有一条来自艾比·蒂尔福德的粉丝发现。

763
00:36:38.320 --> 00:36:44.520
OK, she says in launch party around 16 minutes, 25 seconds.
好的，她说在《发布会》那一集大约16分25秒的时候。

764
00:36:44.820 --> 00:36:47.120
So this was a moment from last week's breakdown.
这是上周解析中的一个片段。

765
00:36:47.840 --> 00:36:50.620
Angela says she's been working on the party for two weeks.
安吉拉说她已经为派对筹备了两周。

766
00:36:51.320 --> 00:36:57.320
But now at 25 minutes, 21 seconds, she says she's been planning it for three weeks.
但现在在25分21秒时，她说她已经筹备了三周。

767
00:36:58.340 --> 00:37:00.980
Is this just Angela being dramatic?
这只是安吉拉在演戏吗？

768
00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:01.560
What is this?
这是怎么回事？

769
00:37:01.620 --> 00:37:03.100
This is a bit of a continuity catch.
这是一个小小的连贯性漏洞。

770
00:37:03.320 --> 00:37:04.060
And I looked.
我查了一下。

771
00:37:04.200 --> 00:37:04.720
She's right.
她是正确的。

772
00:37:04.960 --> 00:37:06.160
Oh, no, she's right.
哦，不，她是正确的。

773
00:37:06.280 --> 00:37:07.300
It's a continuity error.
这是一个连贯性错误。

774
00:37:07.520 --> 00:37:11.840
And maybe we can justify it by saying that Angela feels very put upon all of a sudden.
也许我们可以解释说，安吉拉突然感到压力很大。

775
00:37:11.840 --> 00:37:13.780
So maybe she's exaggerating.
所以她可能是在夸大其词。

776
00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:15.980
And I have an improv catch.
我还有一个即兴发挥的发现。

777
00:37:16.140 --> 00:37:18.940
I improvised the last line as I walked away.
我走开时即兴说了最后一句台词。

778
00:37:19.160 --> 00:37:22.180
I said, and Kevin had Greek food for lunch again.
我说，凯文午餐又吃了希腊菜。

779
00:37:22.400 --> 00:37:23.480
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

780
00:37:23.600 --> 00:37:24.340
That was an improv?
那是即兴发挥的？

781
00:37:24.340 --> 00:37:26.840
Yes, that was an improv.
是的，那是即兴发挥的。

782
00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:31.900
And what you don't see is that Matt Soane cut over to Brian as Kevin.
你没看到的是，马特·索恩切到了布莱恩扮演的凯文的镜头。

783
00:37:32.080 --> 00:37:43.280
And he was like, hey, I love that your character's go to is always to find some subtle way to insult Kevin.
他说，嘿，我喜欢你角色的习惯，总是能找到一些微妙的方式来羞辱凯文。

784
00:37:43.720 --> 00:37:48.520
Yeah, because he has a constant annoyance for her constant all day long.
是啊，因为她整天都对他感到厌烦。

785
00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:51.580
I'm telling you, I think she requested the glass partition.
我跟你说，我觉得玻璃隔断是她要求的。

786
00:37:52.420 --> 00:37:53.700
He drives her crazy.
他快把她逼疯了。

787
00:37:53.960 --> 00:37:54.800
She needed a barrier.
她需要一道屏障。

788
00:37:55.860 --> 00:37:58.740
Well, now we have a little bit of Pam sass coming up.
好了，接下来我们要看到一点帕姆的傲娇表现了。

789
00:37:58.960 --> 00:38:00.400
The pizza guy has arrived.
披萨外卖员到了。

790
00:38:00.600 --> 00:38:04.380
And Pam calls Michael and says, hey, the pizza by Alfredo guy is here.
帕姆给迈克尔打电话说，嘿，阿尔弗雷多披萨店的人来了。

791
00:38:04.760 --> 00:38:06.660
Michael says, you don't have to say it like that.
迈克尔说，你没必要那样说。

792
00:38:06.820 --> 00:38:08.600
And Pam says, I said it normal.
帕姆说，我说话很正常。

793
00:38:09.520 --> 00:38:11.220
I did say it normal.
我确实说得很正常。

794
00:38:11.560 --> 00:38:15.960
I know, but I just love that Pam, this is this new I'm in love, Pam.
我知道，但我就是喜欢现在的帕姆，这是坠入爱河后的帕姆。

795
00:38:16.200 --> 00:38:17.140
I give zero Fs.
我根本不在乎。

796
00:38:17.240 --> 00:38:18.200
I say what I think.
我想到什么就说什么。

797
00:38:18.560 --> 00:38:19.660
And I loved it.
我很喜欢这一点。

798
00:38:19.660 --> 00:38:22.200
But yes, the pizza guy is here.
但没错，披萨外卖员到了。

799
00:38:22.600 --> 00:38:27.240
And oh, man, this starts a whole Michael spiral.
天哪，这引发了迈克尔的一连串崩溃。

800
00:38:27.560 --> 00:38:32.820
Everything he is feeling about Ryan and feeling left out and not treated fairly.
他对于瑞安的所有感受，以及那种被冷落、没被公平对待的感觉。

801
00:38:32.860 --> 00:38:39.820
He is going to pile on this poor teenager who's just a pizza delivery guy.
他打算去为难这个可怜的青少年，对方只不过是个送披萨的。

802
00:38:40.240 --> 00:38:47.140
Yeah, he is mad because the pizza kid will not accept his half off coupon for all of the pizzas.
没错，他很生气，因为那个送披萨的孩子不肯接受他那张针对所有披萨的半价优惠券。

803
00:38:48.020 --> 00:38:52.300
He explains, you can have half off two pizzas, but not all of the pizzas.
他解释说，你可以买两份披萨半价，但不能所有披萨都半价。

804
00:38:52.560 --> 00:38:55.660
And Michael is like, it doesn't say that anywhere on the coupon.
迈克尔却觉得，优惠券上根本没写这些。

805
00:38:56.080 --> 00:38:58.740
And the pizza kid is like, I don't know what to tell you.
而送披萨的孩子表示，我也不知道该怎么跟你说。

806
00:38:59.060 --> 00:39:03.960
I mean, he's basically like, if I give you half off all these pizzas and I go back, I'm going to get in trouble.
我的意思是，他基本上是说，如果我给你们所有这些披萨都打半价，我回去会惹麻烦的。

807
00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:07.420
This is not I mean, it's not my decision to make.
这并不是，我是说，这不是我能决定的。

808
00:39:07.420 --> 00:39:11.840
I can't authorize your new use of this coupon.
我没法批准你这种新的优惠券用法。

809
00:39:12.140 --> 00:39:19.620
Well, and listen, the pizza guy does have a little bit of that teenage sass, though, because he's like, not my problem.
嗯，听着，那个送披萨的确实有点青少年的傲慢，因为他表现得一副“这不关我事”的样子。

810
00:39:19.920 --> 00:39:22.340
A little bit full teenager sass.
确实有点青少年的傲慢劲儿。

811
00:39:22.580 --> 00:39:24.960
Listen, this truly isn't his problem.
听着，这确实不是他的问题。

812
00:39:24.960 --> 00:39:26.620
And Michael needs to lighten up.
迈克尔需要放轻松点。

813
00:39:26.620 --> 00:39:30.160
But the kid is also kind of an ass.
但那孩子也确实有点混蛋。

814
00:39:30.620 --> 00:39:31.500
For sure.
确实。

815
00:39:31.900 --> 00:39:40.640
Well, Michael's response to this is to have Dwight lock him in the conference room until he decides to honor the coupon.
好吧，迈克尔对此的反应是让德怀特把他锁在会议室里，直到他决定接受那张优惠券为止。

816
00:39:40.960 --> 00:39:42.360
It's so irrational.
这太不理智了。

817
00:39:42.620 --> 00:39:47.600
He says that he needs to learn to about respect and accountability and follow through.
他说那孩子需要学习什么是尊重、责任感和贯彻执行。

818
00:39:47.820 --> 00:39:49.280
He's saying all this crazy stuff.
他一直在说这些疯狂的话。

819
00:39:49.280 --> 00:39:51.600
And then, of course, he really loses it.
然后，当然，他真的失控了。

820
00:39:51.720 --> 00:39:54.760
And it's like the guy is like, this is stupid.
那孩子觉得这太蠢了。

821
00:39:54.880 --> 00:39:57.180
And he's like, you don't even know what stupid is.
迈克尔却说，你根本不知道什么才叫蠢。

822
00:39:57.360 --> 00:39:59.780
It's about to get all stupid up in here.
这里马上就要变得不可理喻了。

823
00:40:00.340 --> 00:40:02.680
This is such an outrageous storyline.
这剧情真是太离谱了。

824
00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:08.780
As I was watching this episode, I just kept thinking, I can't believe we are doing this storyline.
我在看这一集的时候，一直在想，真不敢相信我们竟然拍了这段剧情。

825
00:40:09.300 --> 00:40:10.540
It is so funny.
这太搞笑了。

826
00:40:10.880 --> 00:40:12.460
It is really broad.
这真的很夸张。

827
00:40:12.700 --> 00:40:13.480
It's really broad.
真的很夸张。

828
00:40:13.620 --> 00:40:17.500
But yet at the same time, you kind of believe that Michael would do it.
但与此同时，你又觉得迈克尔确实干得出这种事。

829
00:40:17.500 --> 00:40:20.320
That Michael would be like, no, you're going to stay here and you're going to learn a lesson.
迈克尔会说，不，你得留在这儿，你得学点教训。

830
00:40:20.520 --> 00:40:24.380
And everyone around him is like, you have just kidnapped someone.
而周围的人都在说，你这可是绑架了别人。

831
00:40:24.640 --> 00:40:27.020
You are currently holding someone hostage.
你现在是在扣押人质。

832
00:40:27.220 --> 00:40:27.980
And he's like, no, no, no.
他却说，不，不，不。

833
00:40:28.100 --> 00:40:29.100
I'm teaching him a lesson.
我是在给他上一课。

834
00:40:29.800 --> 00:40:30.460
Well, yeah.
好吧，确实。

835
00:40:30.700 --> 00:40:42.240
Kevin, Oscar, Stanley, they have all started researching kidnapping and accomplices to see if they can be charged as, you know, accessories to Michael's crime.
凯文、奥斯卡、斯坦利，他们都开始研究绑架和同谋罪，看看他们是否会被指控为迈克尔罪行的从犯。

836
00:40:42.480 --> 00:40:44.500
But this is what Michael does.
但这正是迈克尔的作风。

837
00:40:44.500 --> 00:40:53.480
You know, it's like in the episode when he drives his car in the lake, he takes it out on the guy who ate the turtles from the gift basket.
你知道，就像他开车冲进湖里那一集一样，他把气撒在那个吃了礼品篮里乌龟的人身上。

838
00:40:54.580 --> 00:40:58.740
He always, like, shifts the blame and responsibility.
他总是这样，推卸责任。

839
00:40:58.740 --> 00:41:05.140
If Michael is embarrassed or if Michael is upset about something, he takes it out on a very ordinary moment.
如果迈克尔感到尴尬或者对某事感到心烦，他就会把气撒在一些非常普通的事情上。

840
00:41:05.140 --> 00:41:06.360
And it's so funny.
这太搞笑了。

841
00:41:07.500 --> 00:41:10.080
And we've all sort of been there, right?
我们都有过这种经历，对吧？

842
00:41:10.200 --> 00:41:12.300
We've all had that displaced anger.
我们都有过那种迁怒于人的时候。

843
00:41:12.860 --> 00:41:18.700
Like, I'll never forget one time my dad had, he had ordered this new barbecue grill.
比如，我永远忘不了有一次我爸订了一个新的烧烤架。

844
00:41:18.940 --> 00:41:22.940
And Jenna, this guy in my hometown makes them, you know, like a smoker.
珍娜，我老家有个家伙专门做这个，你知道，就是那种熏烤炉。

845
00:41:23.160 --> 00:41:24.060
And he's a welder.
他是个焊工。

846
00:41:24.220 --> 00:41:26.560
And he made my dad this smoker.
他给我爸做了这个熏烤炉。

847
00:41:26.560 --> 00:41:29.900
And it took him a while because he makes it, you know, by hand.
花了他不少时间，因为你知道，那是他手工制作的。

848
00:41:29.900 --> 00:41:30.920
He's out there welding.
他就在那儿焊接。

849
00:41:31.280 --> 00:41:32.940
And my dad went to get it.
然后我爸去取它。

850
00:41:32.980 --> 00:41:39.020
And he got a flatbed trailer to put it on and pull it behind our truck.
他找了一辆平板拖车把它装上，然后用我们的卡车拖回来。

851
00:41:39.180 --> 00:41:40.620
He was so excited.
他当时特别兴奋。

852
00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:42.620
We'd waited so long.
我们等了太久了。

853
00:41:42.780 --> 00:41:46.220
And he's driving down the driveway with it.
他正开着车把它往车道上运。

854
00:41:46.640 --> 00:41:54.640
And he didn't, like, factor in, like, the overhang of the carport and dented in the new smoker.
结果他没考虑到车棚的顶棚，把新买的熏烤炉给撞凹了。

855
00:41:54.640 --> 00:41:55.620
Oh, no.
噢，不。

856
00:41:55.980 --> 00:41:56.100
Yeah.
是啊。

857
00:41:56.500 --> 00:41:59.080
And for whatever reason, he got up.
不知怎么的，他下车了。

858
00:41:59.320 --> 00:42:00.380
We were all like, don't say anything.
我们当时都心想，千万别说话。

859
00:42:00.500 --> 00:42:00.980
Don't say anything.
什么都别说。

860
00:42:01.140 --> 00:42:01.980
He got out of the car.
他从车里出来了。

861
00:42:02.040 --> 00:42:07.280
And he was like, if that tree hadn't been there, then he was, like, going to cut down the tree.
他说，如果不是那棵树挡着，他本来打算把那棵树砍了。

862
00:42:07.520 --> 00:42:09.800
And my mom was like, it's not the tree's fault.
我妈就说，这又不是树的错。

863
00:42:10.080 --> 00:42:12.310
It's part of it.
这是其中的一部分。

864
00:42:12.430 --> 00:42:16.910
You know, but we've all had these moments where we're so, like, upset and irrationally.
你知道，我们都有过那种非常心烦意乱、不可理喻的时刻。

865
00:42:17.050 --> 00:42:18.230
We're like, that's it.
我们当时就想，就这样吧。

866
00:42:18.730 --> 00:42:19.610
It's the tree.
就是那棵树。

867
00:42:20.170 --> 00:42:21.030
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

868
00:42:21.190 --> 00:42:24.790
Well, speaking of tree, we were all set to get our Christmas tree.
说到树，我们本来都准备好去买圣诞树了。

869
00:42:25.110 --> 00:42:25.290
Yeah.
是啊。

870
00:42:25.290 --> 00:42:28.010
On this one day, we were going to set up the Christmas tree.
那天我们本来打算把圣诞树立起来的。

871
00:42:28.330 --> 00:42:30.290
And I can't remember what happened.
我不记得发生了什么事。

872
00:42:30.510 --> 00:42:32.150
It was, like, something.
好像是出了点什么状况。

873
00:42:32.150 --> 00:42:33.370
And it was the night before.
就在前一天晚上。

874
00:42:33.630 --> 00:42:37.330
And I said to Lee, I said, so we're getting up early in the morning.
我对李说，我们明天一早就要起床。

875
00:42:37.450 --> 00:42:38.350
We're going to go get our tree.
我们要去买我们的树。

876
00:42:38.510 --> 00:42:39.770
We're going to decorate the tree tomorrow.
我们明天要装饰圣诞树。

877
00:42:40.010 --> 00:42:42.710
And he said very casually, well, I don't know.
他当时很随意地说，嗯，我不知道。

878
00:42:42.830 --> 00:42:44.430
I mean, tomorrow or another day.
我的意思是，明天还是改天。

879
00:42:45.230 --> 00:42:47.790
And I was like, what?
我当时就想，什么？

880
00:42:48.390 --> 00:42:49.210
It's going to.
一定会装饰的。

881
00:42:51.770 --> 00:42:54.510
And I, like, I was, like, a mess.
我当时整个人都崩溃了。

882
00:42:54.510 --> 00:42:56.570
I was, like, screaming and yelling.
我大喊大叫。

883
00:42:56.590 --> 00:42:57.590
And he sat there.
而他就坐在那儿。

884
00:42:57.710 --> 00:43:02.810
And then he looked at me and he said, babe, is it really about the tree or something else
然后他看着我说，宝贝，这真的是因为圣诞树，还是因为别的事情

885
00:43:02.810 --> 00:43:03.350
going on?
正在发生？

886
00:43:03.490 --> 00:43:03.610
Yeah.
是啊。

887
00:43:04.330 --> 00:43:05.870
And then I was like, oh, yeah.
然后我才反应过来，哦，对啊。

888
00:43:06.370 --> 00:43:13.410
It was that the tree was the one Christmas tradition that I knew we could do in a pandemic.
因为圣诞树是我唯一确定在疫情期间我们还能坚持的圣诞传统。

889
00:43:13.410 --> 00:43:18.650
I could still put a tree in my house and I could decorate it and we could drink hot chocolate.
我依然可以在家里放一棵树，装饰它，我们还可以喝热巧克力。

890
00:43:18.970 --> 00:43:24.150
I couldn't do any of the other gatherings or parties or seeing of people or seeing my
我没法参加任何其他的聚会、派对，也没法见人，或者见我的

891
00:43:24.150 --> 00:43:24.710
family.
家人。

892
00:43:25.650 --> 00:43:28.770
All of my gift exchanges turned into Zoom exchanges.
我所有的礼物交换都变成了线上视频交换。

893
00:43:29.170 --> 00:43:34.330
And I had been holding on to this tradition of putting on Christmas music and decorating
我一直坚持着放圣诞音乐、装饰

894
00:43:34.330 --> 00:43:34.950
our tree.
我们圣诞树的传统。

895
00:43:34.950 --> 00:43:41.470
And the idea that we might not do it on that Saturday, but maybe we do it Sunday.
一想到我们可能没法在那个周六做这件事，也许得等到周日。

896
00:43:41.750 --> 00:43:46.670
I was like, I had a real, real big reaction.
我当时反应真的、真的特别大。

897
00:43:47.490 --> 00:43:47.670
Yeah.
是啊。

898
00:43:48.010 --> 00:43:48.830
So guess what?
所以你猜怎么着？

