在Instagram上，他的名字就是他的全名，Kevin McHale。

1335
01:07:28.340 --> 01:07:31.140
That's Kevin, M-C-H-A-L-E.
那是Kevin，M-C-H-A-L-E。

1336
01:07:31.380 --> 01:07:34.280
And on Twitter, he is Druid Dude.
在Twitter上，他是Druid Dude。

1337
01:07:34.920 --> 01:07:37.460
D-R-U-I-D-D-U-D-E.
D-R-U-I-D-D-U-D-E。

1338
01:07:37.460 --> 01:07:43.520
Well, now, Angela, we have my other favorite scene from this episode coming up with you
好了，安吉拉，接下来要播的是这一集中我最喜欢的另一个场景，

1339
01:07:43.520 --> 01:07:44.120
in it again.
你又出镜了。

1340
01:07:44.540 --> 01:07:47.960
I love that scene with you and Michael where he's giving you all of the instructions.
我喜欢你和迈克尔的那场戏，他当时在给你下各种指示。

1341
01:07:47.960 --> 01:07:58.260
And I love when Andy comes over to serenade Angela over speakerphone with his acapella pals.
我也喜欢安迪过来用免提电话和他的阿卡贝拉伙伴们给安吉拉唱小夜曲的那段。

1342
01:07:59.020 --> 01:08:01.760
This was, did you say acapella pals?
这是，你是说阿卡贝拉伙伴们？

1343
01:08:02.220 --> 01:08:03.300
Acapella pals.
阿卡贝拉伙伴们。

1344
01:08:03.880 --> 01:08:04.860
Acapella pals.
阿卡贝拉伙伴们。

1345
01:08:04.860 --> 01:08:06.480
His acapella pals.
他的阿卡贝拉伙伴们。

1346
01:08:06.680 --> 01:08:07.860
His acapella pals.
他的阿卡贝拉伙伴们。

1347
01:08:09.280 --> 01:08:10.100
Aca what?
阿卡什么？

1348
01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:11.240
My acapella pals.
我的阿卡贝拉伙伴们。

1349
01:08:11.640 --> 01:08:12.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1350
01:08:12.280 --> 01:08:14.380
This scene was so much fun to do.
拍这场戏真的太有趣了。

1351
01:08:15.060 --> 01:08:18.680
And oh my gosh, more went into it than you'll know.
天哪，这背后的付出远超你们的想象。

1352
01:08:18.840 --> 01:08:22.160
I mean, it was pretty like a tech heavy moment.
我的意思是，那确实是一个技术含量很高的时刻。

1353
01:08:22.840 --> 01:08:23.920
Oh, for sure.
噢，那肯定的。

1354
01:08:24.260 --> 01:08:30.400
Well, we actually asked Jen, how did she come up with this idea for the serenade?
嗯，我们其实问过珍，她是怎么想到这个小夜曲的点子的？

1355
01:08:30.500 --> 01:08:31.840
Or how did she pitch this idea?
或者说她是怎么提出这个想法的？

1356
01:08:31.840 --> 01:08:34.520
Because this was brilliant and so charming.
因为这太精彩、太迷人了。

1357
01:08:34.740 --> 01:08:36.240
And here's what she had to say.
以下是她的回答。

1358
01:08:36.240 --> 01:08:42.260
I remember pitching to Greg that Andy could sing, take a chance on me to Angela with speakerphone
我记得我向格雷格提议，安迪可以对着免提电话给安吉拉唱《Take a Chance on Me》，

1359
01:08:42.260 --> 01:08:43.320
backup singers.
还要有伴唱。

1360
01:08:43.920 --> 01:08:45.140
And Greg was like, cool, cool.
格雷格当时说，酷，酷。

1361
01:08:45.240 --> 01:08:47.760
Go tell Ed so we can start thinking about how he'd want to sing it.
去告诉艾德，这样我们就能开始考虑他想怎么唱了。

1362
01:08:48.560 --> 01:08:50.780
And I walked down to Ed's trailer.
于是我走到艾德的拖车前。

1363
01:08:50.780 --> 01:08:53.560
And I'm just awkward in general.
我本来就有点笨拙。

1364
01:08:53.840 --> 01:09:01.220
But then also, I had a bit of a fangirl thing because I loved Ed on The Daily Show.
而且当时我还有点小粉丝心态，因为我超爱看艾德在《每日秀》里的表现。

1365
01:09:01.260 --> 01:09:03.440
And I was still so excited that he was on The Office.
他能来《办公室》演戏，我当时依然非常兴奋。

1366
01:09:03.620 --> 01:09:08.720
So I just awkwardly knocked on his trailer door and told him, hey, we're thinking about
所以我笨拙地敲了敲他的拖车门，告诉他，嘿，我们打算让

1367
01:09:08.720 --> 01:09:10.760
having Andy sing, take a chance on me to Angela.
安迪对着电话给安吉拉唱《Take a Chance on Me》。

1368
01:09:11.540 --> 01:09:13.800
And we just wanted you to start thinking about the song.
我们只是想让你先琢磨一下这首歌。

1369
01:09:13.940 --> 01:09:14.560
He's like, what song?
他问，什么歌？

1370
01:09:14.680 --> 01:09:17.260
I said, take a chance on me, Mamma Mia, Abba.
我说，《Take a Chance on Me》，《妈妈咪呀》里的，阿巴乐队的歌。

1371
01:09:18.480 --> 01:09:20.860
And he didn't know the song.
结果他竟然不知道这首歌。

1372
01:09:21.020 --> 01:09:23.820
And I'm thinking, oh, God, how can you not know the song?
我当时心想，天哪，你怎么可能不知道这首歌？

1373
01:09:24.040 --> 01:09:26.640
Maybe slightly predicting the horror that was about to come.
或许我当时就隐约预感到了即将到来的“灾难”。

1374
01:09:27.520 --> 01:09:29.640
And he's like, how does it go?
他问，这歌怎么唱？

1375
01:09:29.840 --> 01:09:31.620
And I am a terrible singer.
而我唱歌极其难听。

1376
01:09:31.740 --> 01:09:32.580
I cannot sing at all.
我根本就不会唱歌。

1377
01:09:32.580 --> 01:09:38.360
And so I was like, oh, you know, it's like, remember Mamma Mia?
所以我当时就说，噢，你知道的，就是，记得《妈妈咪呀》吗？

1378
01:09:38.800 --> 01:09:40.380
And did you know the song?
你难道不知道这首歌吗？

1379
01:09:40.600 --> 01:09:43.300
And I just tried to figure out how to say it without singing it.
我当时绞尽脑汁想在不唱出来的情况下把旋律表达清楚。

1380
01:09:43.420 --> 01:09:46.860
And then we ended up walking around the parking lot.
后来我们干脆在停车场边走边聊。

1381
01:09:46.860 --> 01:09:50.860
And I had to sing, take a chance on me to Ed.
我不得不对着艾德唱了那首《Take a Chance on Me》。

1382
01:09:51.180 --> 01:09:56.200
And it was so embarrassing, but so lovely.
那真是太尴尬了，但也太可爱了。

1383
01:09:56.460 --> 01:09:58.060
He was so wonderful about it.
他对此表现得非常棒。

1384
01:09:58.280 --> 01:10:00.780
And I love that scene so much.
我太喜欢那一幕了。

1385
01:10:00.780 --> 01:10:07.900
I just thought he killed it and was so excited that he was able to do such a fantastic job with it.
我觉得他演得太绝了，他能把这一段完成得这么出色，我真的很激动。

1386
01:10:08.040 --> 01:10:08.880
It was just exciting.
那真的太让人兴奋了。

1387
01:10:10.820 --> 01:10:11.740
That would be me.
换做是我肯定不行。

1388
01:10:11.880 --> 01:10:17.440
I'd be so nervous if all of a sudden I had to sing something to someone because I hate singing in front of people.
如果我突然得当众给别人唱歌，我会紧张死的，因为我讨厌在别人面前唱歌。

1389
01:10:17.600 --> 01:10:23.000
I love to belt it out, you know, at home, in the shower or like just in the kitchen with the kids.
我喜欢在家里大声唱，你知道，在淋浴时，或者就在厨房里陪孩子们的时候。

1390
01:10:23.000 --> 01:10:32.520
But if I had to like, you know, oh, my God, like have someone like Ed or like Steve or someone be like, OK, how does that go?
但如果我必须，你知道，天哪，如果像艾德或史蒂夫这样的人问我：好吧，那歌怎么唱？

1391
01:10:32.660 --> 01:10:34.740
I'd be so nervous and embarrassed.
我会紧张到尴尬得要命。

1392
01:10:36.380 --> 01:10:45.300
Well, we also got a lot of fan questions from Jen Reynolds, Sarah Thorup, Stephen Jackson, Roxanne Hoffman and Becca Harrington.
嗯，我们还收到了来自珍·雷诺兹、莎拉·索鲁普、斯蒂芬·杰克逊、罗克珊·霍夫曼和贝卡·哈林顿的许多粉丝提问。

1393
01:10:45.760 --> 01:10:50.540
They wanted to know who sang the backup on the telephone for Andy.
他们想知道是谁在电话里为安迪伴唱的。

1394
01:10:51.380 --> 01:10:52.900
How was that accomplished?
那是怎么实现的？

1395
01:10:53.280 --> 01:10:56.620
Were they actually on the line or was it pre-recorded?
他们是真的在电话线上实时演唱，还是预先录制好的？

1396
01:10:57.060 --> 01:10:59.980
Oh, Jenna, my memory is we did that in real time.
噢，珍娜，我的记忆是，我们是实时完成的。

1397
01:11:00.040 --> 01:11:02.820
And I'll tell you why, because I had to be there reacting.
我告诉你为什么，因为我必须在现场做出反应。

1398
01:11:03.020 --> 01:11:11.160
And I thought, whatever you do, Angela, you cannot mess this up for these guys, you know, like because they had it all timed out.
我当时心想，安吉拉，不管你做什么，绝对不能搞砸了，因为他们把时间点都卡好了。

1399
01:11:11.160 --> 01:11:13.720
And we actually asked Jen Salata about it.
我们其实也问过珍·萨拉塔关于这件事的情况。

1400
01:11:13.840 --> 01:11:15.180
And this is what she had to say.
以下是她的回答。

1401
01:11:15.360 --> 01:11:20.740
One of the singers we were so lucky to get for the acapella Take a Chance on Me was John Michael Higgins.
我们在录制阿卡贝拉版《Take a Chance on Me》时，有幸请到的歌手之一是约翰·迈克尔·希金斯。

1402
01:11:20.980 --> 01:11:23.220
You'll know him from Christopher Guest movies.
你们应该在克里斯托弗·盖斯特的电影里见过他。

1403
01:11:23.220 --> 01:11:24.240
He's just brilliant.
他简直太棒了。

1404
01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:25.940
And so we were super, super excited.
所以我们当时超级超级兴奋。

1405
01:11:26.240 --> 01:11:29.120
I don't know who the other singer was.
我不记得另一位歌手是谁了。

1406
01:11:29.120 --> 01:11:31.980
So I tried to track it down and I was unsuccessful.
我试着去查了一下，但没查到。

1407
01:11:31.980 --> 01:11:46.720
Um, we, I believe we recorded it on the day in that, um, John and whoever else, maybe besides John, were in the little office that the writers used to hang out on, on set.
嗯，我相信我们是在片场编剧们平时待的小办公室里录的，当时约翰和另外的人——除了约翰之外可能还有别人——都在那儿。

1408
01:11:46.720 --> 01:11:50.300
And they called in and sang through the speakerphones.
他们打来电话，对着免提扬声器唱完了整首歌。

1409
01:11:50.480 --> 01:11:59.900
And then I'm sure we recorded a clean version, too, of it, um, uh, not through the speakerphones so that we could have it in the mix and then just, uh,
后来我肯定我们也录了一个清晰的版本，不是通过免提录的，这样我们就能把它放进混音里，然后，呃，

1410
01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:02.560
make sure that we got the sound quality great.
确保音质达到最佳效果。

1411
01:12:02.840 --> 01:12:04.980
But, uh, it was a really fun day.
但那真是非常有趣的一天。

1412
01:12:05.260 --> 01:12:07.420
I just thought that they killed it.
我觉得他们唱得太绝了。

1413
01:12:07.420 --> 01:12:19.660
Well, I remember that, Angela, because I remember listening to Ed and those guys practicing before they divided up and went into the sort of speakerphone situation.
安吉拉，我记得那件事，因为我记得在他们分开去录免提版本之前，听过艾德他们练习。

1414
01:12:19.880 --> 01:12:20.280
Right, right.
没错，没错。

1415
01:12:20.700 --> 01:12:22.620
But it was a big deal.
但这确实是一件大事。

1416
01:12:22.620 --> 01:12:27.880
And what a big get for just this voice on the phone that has gone completely uncredited.
而且能请到这样一位在电话里献声却完全没有署名的歌手，真是太难得了。

1417
01:12:28.140 --> 01:12:28.800
I know.
我知道。

1418
01:12:28.920 --> 01:12:30.900
And I am such a fan of John's.
而且我是约翰的超级粉丝。

1419
01:12:30.980 --> 01:12:33.020
Like, he is such a comedic genius.
他简直是个喜剧天才。

1420
01:12:33.880 --> 01:12:40.660
And, and, and he and Ed and how they put this all together and did it was so fantastic.
还有他、艾德，他们把这一切组合在一起的方式真是太棒了。

1421
01:12:41.100 --> 01:12:43.220
I loved every second of it.
我享受其中的每一秒。

1422
01:12:43.500 --> 01:12:48.940
It was hard for me not to fully smile because it was so charming and delightful.
我很难忍住不笑出来，因为它太迷人、太令人愉悦了。

1423
01:12:49.380 --> 01:12:52.120
And, you know, Angela's trying not to tip her hand too much.
而且，你知道，安吉拉当时在努力不表现得太明显。

1424
01:12:52.240 --> 01:12:55.460
She only has a very slight smile at like one or two parts.
她只有在一两个地方露出了非常轻微的笑容。

1425
01:12:55.640 --> 01:12:55.800
Right?
对吧？

1426
01:12:56.280 --> 01:12:56.460
Yep.
没错。

1427
01:12:56.820 --> 01:13:03.000
But, um, I just, I have such fond memories of this and I just felt like we had to hear it.
总之，我对这段经历有非常美好的回忆，我觉得我们必须听听看。

1428
01:13:03.720 --> 01:13:09.420
If you change your mind, I'll be first in line.
如果你回心转意，我会排在第一个。

1429
01:13:09.720 --> 01:13:11.600
Honey, I'm still free.
亲爱的，我依然单身。

1430
01:13:12.200 --> 01:13:13.940
Take a chance on me.
给我一个机会吧。

1431
01:13:14.220 --> 01:13:16.980
If you need me, let me know.
如果你需要我，就告诉我。

1432
01:13:17.080 --> 01:13:18.520
Gonna be around.
我会一直在你身边。

1433
01:13:18.860 --> 01:13:21.340
If you got no place to go.
如果你无处可去。

1434
01:13:21.540 --> 01:13:22.940
If you're feeling down.
如果你感到失落。

1435
01:13:23.340 --> 01:13:25.380
If you're all alone.
如果你孤身一人。

1436
01:13:25.680 --> 01:13:28.440
When the pretty birds have flown.
当美丽的鸟儿已远走高飞。

1437
01:13:28.640 --> 01:13:30.040
Honey, I'm still free.
亲爱的，我依然单身。

1438
01:13:30.440 --> 01:13:32.420
Take a chance on me.
给我一个机会吧。

1439
01:13:32.420 --> 01:13:35.640
Gonna do my very beSt.
我会尽我所能。

1440
01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:37.160
And that ain't no lie.
这绝非虚言。

1441
01:13:37.560 --> 01:13:40.040
If you put me to the teSt.
如果你给我考验。

1442
01:13:40.040 --> 01:13:41.600
If you let me try.
如果你让我尝试。

1443
01:13:41.920 --> 01:13:44.100
Take a chance on me.
给我一个机会吧。

1444
01:13:46.190 --> 01:13:48.290
That's all I ask of you, Angela.
安吉拉，我要求的仅此而已。

1445
01:13:49.910 --> 01:13:54.410
I mean, I mean, come on, how they harmonized at the end like that.
我是说，天哪，他们最后那段和声处理得太好了。

1446
01:13:54.850 --> 01:13:55.250
All right.
好吧。

1447
01:13:55.250 --> 01:13:56.930
I got goosebumps listening to that.
听得我起了一身鸡皮疙瘩。

1448
01:13:57.110 --> 01:13:58.190
I got a little choked up.
我有点哽咽了。

1449
01:13:58.570 --> 01:14:01.450
I don't know if I just miss Ed a lot.
我不知道是不是因为我太想念艾德了。

1450
01:14:01.450 --> 01:14:03.990
And he's so charming in this scene.
他在这一幕里真是太迷人了。

1451
01:14:04.150 --> 01:14:04.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1452
01:14:04.590 --> 01:14:06.530
Or if it's just the time we're in.
又或者是我们所处的这个时代使然。

1453
01:14:08.010 --> 01:14:09.070
I don't know.
我不知道。

1454
01:14:09.070 --> 01:14:13.810
I've also just fallen in love with Andy during this rewatch.
这次重温，我也爱上了安迪这个角色。

1455
01:14:13.810 --> 01:14:19.330
You know, we've talked about how I have this new appreciation for Ryan.
你知道，我们之前聊过，我现在对瑞安有了新的欣赏。

1456
01:14:19.610 --> 01:14:20.070
Right.
没错。

1457
01:14:20.270 --> 01:14:24.750
But I also just have been loving the character of Andy and his journey.
但我最近也一直很喜欢安迪这个角色以及他的成长历程。

1458
01:14:26.190 --> 01:14:27.630
But I don't know, Angela.
但我不知道，安吉拉。

1459
01:14:27.830 --> 01:14:33.690
I also have to say, I know I mentioned that the weight of my heart is to put together a grill and break down the box.
我还要说，虽然我提过我心里的重头戏是组装烤架和拆掉包装盒。

1460
01:14:33.810 --> 01:14:43.310
But I think that if there was a guy that I actually was not that interested in, if he did this, I would be like, okay.
但我觉得，如果是一个我本来没那么感兴趣的男生，他要是做了这种事，我也会觉得，好吧。

1461
01:14:43.750 --> 01:14:44.310
All right.
行吧。

1462
01:14:44.310 --> 01:14:47.410
I, it is so sweet.
我，这真的太贴心了。

1463
01:14:47.530 --> 01:14:49.570
It's so, so charming.
真的非常、非常有魅力。

1464
01:14:49.970 --> 01:14:54.850
You know, my husband is a really good singer and he doesn't really sing around people.
你知道，我丈夫唱歌很好听，但他平时不太会在别人面前唱。

1465
01:14:55.190 --> 01:15:01.510
But when we first started dating, we went out and there was karaoke and I didn't really know the side of him.
但我们刚开始约会时，有次出去玩正好有卡拉OK，我当时还不了解他那一面。

1466
01:15:01.650 --> 01:15:02.870
He's like an acapella guy.
他是个阿卡贝拉爱好者。

1467
01:15:03.070 --> 01:15:05.210
And he got up and sang Journey.
他上台唱了Journey乐队的歌。

1468
01:15:06.450 --> 01:15:10.810
And he brought down the bar and I was like, oh my gosh.
他把全场都震住了，我当时心想，天哪。

1469
01:15:11.470 --> 01:15:12.290
That is amazing.
太棒了。

1470
01:15:13.490 --> 01:15:17.130
But it was just so, so sweet in this moment.
但这时刻真的太甜、太甜了。

1471
01:15:17.390 --> 01:15:20.230
Andy, you know, and Andy will go on to sing to Angela again.
安迪，你知道，安迪之后还会再为安吉拉唱歌。

1472
01:15:20.670 --> 01:15:25.550
But you know, he must really like her if he's going to bust out the acapella group.
但你知道，如果他都要把阿卡贝拉组合搬出来了，那他肯定真的很喜欢她。

